  "notes": "hoh does not reproduce: the statutory rule (floor the INCREASE over the 2024 base to a multiple of $50) gives 24,175 where Rev. Proc. 2025-32 section 4.14(1) publishes 24,150. Residual +$25, recorded not fixed. This residual does NOT depend on the index value: 24,150 - 23,625 = 525 is 10.5 x 50, so no cost-of-living adjustment whatsoever can make the literal rule land on it. 23,625 is a multiple of $25 but not of $50, which makes hoh the ONLY case in the entire M0 parameter set where flooring the increase and flooring the total differ - every statutory bracket base amount is an exact multiple of its status's increment, so no bracket threshold discriminates the two bases for any filing status. The published figure matches the floor-the-total reading. The human decision (decision B2 in docs/verification/m0-hand-verification.md) is whether to implement the statute as written and not reproduce the published hoh figure, or to follow IRS practice and add a FinalAmount value to RoundingRule.basis before seam S1 freezes at M0."
